# The French tune "Ah ! vous dirai-je, maman", as the theme of Mozart's variations K. 265
# (first published Vienna, 1785), from an early Paris print: Porro, n.d., plate 79,
# "Variétés musicales No. II". The tune is traditional; the left hand is Mozart's.
# Played once through: the print repeats bars 1-8 and 9-24.
# This print writes bars 4 and 20 as two Gs, not one long G. The trills in bars 7, 15 and
# 23 are left out (the source format has no ornaments); the notes they sit on are kept.
# Bar 16: Mozart's left hand holds G under C-B; the left hand here plays the moving C-B.
title: Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star
piece: twinkle-twinkle
added: 2026-10-17
source: public-domain
composer: Traditional
composer-died: unknown
first-published: 1785
edition: Early edition, Porro, Paris, n.d., plate 79, Variétés musicales No. II (IMSLP #104399, scan from the Library of Congress)
contributor: left hand (theme of K. 265); Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart; 1791
key: C major
meter: 2/4
# The print has no tempo mark; the tempo is ours.
tempo: 100
summary: The French tune behind the nursery song, as Mozart set it at the head of his variations.
figure: held

